---------------------

This directory should contain all the files necessary to create
Gemini.  The man page "gemini.1i" and the new Gemini user guide
"gemuser.ps" (in PostScript) should explain all new (and old)
features.  There are also two sets of test files in the directory
./tests.

Gemini can be built with the default C compiler cc by running "make".
Gemini can also be compiled with gcc by typing "make CC=gcc".  The
compile flags are set up to produce an optimized version, but with some
assertions included.  The DEBUG compile time flag can be used to enable
the debugging code present in the program.  Refer to the user guide for
more detail.



